From: Diogo Trindade <diogotr7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd-clsh: track the active outputs as a bitmask

The Class-H state is documented as a bit mask of the active outputs, and
wcd9335 tests it that way before reconfiguring the headphone mode when one
headphone channel stops. wcd_clsh_ctrl_set_state() however replaces the
state with whichever output was requested last, on both enable and
disable, so the result of such a test depends on the order in which the
outputs started and stopped rather than on which of them are active.

Set the output's bit when it is enabled and clear it when it is disabled.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
index 62ca22e..e1465b9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
@@ -856,13 +856,14 @@ int wcd_clsh_ctrl_set_state(struct wcd_clsh_ctrl *ctrl,
 	switch (clsh_event) {
 	case WCD_CLSH_EVENT_PRE_DAC:
 		_wcd_clsh_ctrl_set_state(ctrl, nstate, CLSH_REQ_ENABLE, mode);
+		ctrl->state |= nstate;
 		break;
 	case WCD_CLSH_EVENT_POST_PA:
 		_wcd_clsh_ctrl_set_state(ctrl, nstate, CLSH_REQ_DISABLE, mode);
+		ctrl->state &= ~nstate;
 		break;
 	}
 
-	ctrl->state = nstate;
 	ctrl->mode = mode;
 
 	return 0;
